        "sick: 2/3 of pay (Code du travail art. 105) for up to 180 calendar days, the six months after which the employer may end the contract (art. 60). The Code states no day count; 180 is an inference (low). A company may set its own days.",
        "maternity: 14 weeks (98 calendar days) at 2/3 of pay, art. 130 (medium). A 2023 private member's bill proposes full pay; not adopted as far as found.",
        "annual (art. 141): adults 12 working days a year (medium), workers under 18 18 days (low), both +1 day per 5 years of service, after 12 months.",
        "circumstantial: 10 working days a year, not deducted from annual leave (art. 146); own marriage 2, birth of a child 2 (medium). Other events: not found.",
